 to go into would  just be too time-consuming and I'd  rather actually move on and also be able  to look at the larger aspect so I'm  trying because I'm trying to make a very  large touch region in this case but I  also want to go into detail and it's  hard to do those two things at the same  time so you sort of want to compensate  for now having to place too many details  like sheds and at least keep some focus  on the general area and yeah really the  backyards from the from an aerial  perspective still the convincingly  shapes I believe and it's mostly there  so that you can sort of see this shape  develop as you would realistically see  it this is by the way also I think a  really good example of how much more  alive trees make an area view and it's  really important especially when you  just compare how this area looks without  trees and comparing with how it looks  with trees it makes a huge difference  and you can probably make a pretty  poorly designed neighborhood look quite  all right as long as you add enough  foliage to it just something to think  about  I've probably talked about this before  but you know this is also why artists  when they make a render of a pretty bad  building like to put many trees in front  of them because then you don't see how  bad the building is anymore like  architects always like to put all sorts  of trees on the balconies and roof tops  of buildings but it really isn't going  to happen in real life and here we see a  ridiculously overly themed and decorated  splay ground I think I kind of went  overboard we've done as well might want  to keep it a bit more simple and this is  really I feel one of the more  convincingly Dutch cauliflower  neighborhoods which of other subjects  and this is entirely the reason why I  want to get back to the cauliflower  neighborhood perhaps in the future that  still have it in the old town because I  said at some points that I wanted to  maybe remove that cauliflower  neighborhood and which I built and I  think it was episode 4 and actually got  met with a lot of no you shouldn't do  that but I still feel like I might at  some point in the future if I ever find  the time to because at the moment I just  don't feel and has quite the level of  detail which I'm putting in these  neighborhoods I think this is so far my  favorite parts of the entire map and  definitely getting better all the time  when it comes to making these  neighborhoods though there is still of  things that I'm missing but the point is  that at the time that I was making the  old cauliflower type neighborhood in the  large city I didn't quite put as many as  much detail and experience into it as I  did for these houses so now I feel like  even though it's not entirely that bad  there's a huge level of difference in  the quality of the neighborhood so  that's the main reason why I might want  to redo it in the future not because I  don't have a cauliflower neighborhood  anymore I'll definitely keep that idea  but because I just feel like there is  too much of a yeah like a difference  between them which could almost break  you out of your immersion and speaking  of buildings which don't entirely have  the purpose which they supposedly have  this is a crematorium over here but I  really figured it wouldn't be nice to  have it as a crematorium so this might  actually be the City Hall I could call  it that's I guess it sort of looks like  a City Hall ish building I really feel  like it's too fancy to actually be a  crematorium and obviously I was planning  to have a small graveyard over here in  the middle of the town but really felt  like it would be better to decorate it a  little bit add some benches and also a  small football park since otherwise  there wouldn't quite be enough leisure  time in the city and if I ever want to  get to it I may well add a graveyard  more outside with the city but the  moments it doesn't actually have such a  thing so that's also something to think  about anyway that is almost about it for  this episode but I still have a small  flying camera thing at the end of it and  that should show off what the town looks  like in a little bit more  follower bore if that is even a word way  than the time-lapse shots but yeah the  town isn't entirely finished so that's  something to keep in mind there are some  smaller details that I'll still want to  get into in the future and to make sure  buildings I want to add and the other  side of the railroad isn't even finished  yet but this is how the general area is  looking at the moments and I definitely  still need to add a sculpture or  something in the middle of that  roundabouts you don't commonly see  around them outer with nothing in the  middle of it realistically I'd love to  see I'd love to be able to put some  signposts in the middle of it pointing  to what directions lead to where as you  would commonly see but that's something  I can't really do learned how the  roundabouts at the bottom right over  there is sort of just a filler may well  get back to that currently spelled Muse  because I was like couldn't really come  up with anything into place in there so  I just placed whatever I was listening  to at the moment and yeah this is  basically how the area looks and is a  bit more closed shorts actually did add  a couple more bicycles and smaller  details around here as since it just  isn't a Dutch City without random  bicycles thrown about just about  everywhere and part against every wall  that is available and this is really a  type of 60s 70s hobbitses neighborhood  nothing too interesting but I think it  was quite a lot of fun to make it and  the city center like this is the old  center so it has the church and a more  random layouts but it's not the old city  centre in the sense that it's where you  go to shop and where most of the city  life is happening this is sort of the  old part so while it's the most  picturesque probably it isn't the most  alive and like the newer part which is  this over here is more or less supposed  to be more of the modern centre of the  town but yeah that's about it for this  episode so thank you guys for watching a  quite quite a lot of cars actually still  using that shared space place I also  probably overuse the flowers and the  roundabouts yeah but whatever anyway  goodbye
 

